[h1]JSON API[/h1]

A file-based request/response API for Project Zomboid. External tools write request files, the mod processes them and writes responses.

[h2]How It Works[/h2]

External tools write to Lua/jsonapi-queue.txt, the mod processes them and writes responses to Lua/jsonapi-resp-<id>.txt. All responses include a timestamp envelope.

[h2]Build 42.20 Note[/h2]

PZ 42.20 restricts file I/O to .ini/.cfg/.txt/.log extensions only. All files use .txt extension despite containing JSON content.

[h2]Built-in Endpoints[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]sessions[/b] - Connected players with username, character name, and position
[*] [b]status[/b] - Player count and server name
[*] [b]servermsg[/b] - Send a message to all players in global chat
[*] [b]save[/b] - Trigger a world save (includes all player data)
[*] [b]additem[/b] - Give an item to a connected player (instant sync)
[*] [b]playerstats[/b] - Get survival time, zombie kills, and skill levels for a player (or all players)
[/list]

[h2]Installation[/h2]
[olist]
[*] Subscribe to this mod
[*] Add [b]\jsonapi[/b] to your server Mods= line
[*] Add the Workshop ID to WorkshopItems=
[*] Restart the server
[/olist]

[h2]Configuration[/h2]

Sandbox Options > JSON API:
[list]
[*] [b]Poll Interval[/b] - How often to check for requests (default: 2 seconds)
[*] [b]Verbose Logging[/b] - Log each request/response to console
[/list]

[h2]Extensibility[/h2]

Other mods can register custom handlers via JsonAPI.addHandler(). See the GitHub page for full documentation and examples.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] Project Zomboid Build 42.20+
[*] Dedicated servers and singleplayer
[*] Includes server and client components
[*] No dependencies
[*] Works with or without players connected
[/list]

